  "notes": "Printer fleet total battery (8000 Wh) was less than total sintering energy (9949 Wh) for full-dimension blast berm crest (450 m2). To meet the energy budget while keeping landing pad sintering at full dimensions (706.858 m2), blast berm sintering reduced to 218 m2 total (109 m2 per printer). This brings printer work energy to ~7954 Wh plus ~46 Wh travel = ~8000 Wh, within combined battery. All other volumes at full dimensions. Haul tasks split to respect single-robot-per-zone and battery limits. Surveyor tasks sequential globally. Pad excavation split across three excavators sequentially in Z1. Compaction and sintering shared evenly between two compactors and two printers per structure."
